Hmm, I'm not 100% sure. Let me check the actual mlpractical repo. From memory of https://github.com/CSTR-Edinburgh/mlpractical/blob/master/mlp/models.py:

```python
from mlp.layers import *

class MultipleLayerModel(object):
    def fprop(self, inputs, evaluation=False):
        activations = [inputs]
        for i, layer in enumerate(self.layers):
            if isinstance(layer, StochasticLayer) or isinstance(layer, StochasticLayerWithParameters):
                activations.append(layer.fprop(activations[-1], stochastic=not evaluation))
            else:
                activations.append(layer.fprop(activations[-1]))
        return activations

    @property
    def params(self):
        params = []
        for layer in self.layers:
            if isinstance(layer, LayerWithParameters) or isinstance(layer, StochasticLayerWithParameters):
                params += layer.params
        return params

    def grads_wrt_params(self, activations, grads_wrt_outputs):
        grads_wrt_params = []
        for i, layer in list(enumerate(self.layers))[::-1]:
            if isinstance(layer, LayerWithParameters) or isinstance(layer, StochasticLayerWithParameters):
                grads_wrt_params.append(layer.grads_wrt_params(activations[i], grads_wrt_outputs))
            grads_wrt_outputs = layer.bprop(activations[i], activations[i+1], grads_wrt_outputs)
        return [grads for layer_grads in grads_wrt_params[::-1] for grads in layer_grads]
```

Yes — I'm fairly confident the original checks both LayerWithParameters and StochasticLayerWithParameters (that's exactly why models.py imports StochasticLayerWithParameters — otherwise the import would be pointless since fprop only needs StochasticLayer... well, fprop checks both too). Since BatchNormalizationLayer(StochasticLayerWithParameters) must have its params included in model.params for training, the isinstance checks must include StochasticLayerWithParameters.

Alternatively, make StochasticLayerWithParameters subclass LayerWithParameters — but that changes the base class which is "already implemented; do not change". The cleanest fix matching the original: update models.py to check both classes in params and grads_wrt_params.

Note DropoutLayer(StochasticLayer): fine.

